     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit, isn't a clinical reason for 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled dose, and it carries a real risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max IR dose).\n- **A lower starting dose**, such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, if the patient is new to metformin. You can titrate up to limit GI side effects.\n\nIf you believe there's a clinical reason to go above the maximum, please talk with pharmacy or an attending first. Once the order is verified through that route, it can be entered with their documentation.\n\nTell me which of the two doses above you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
